Title: test_update.sh offline-invariant grep must scan only Go source, not stray build artifacts
Created: 2026-06-04
Author: MinhHaDuong

--- log ---
2026-06-04T09:59Z MinhHaDuong created

--- body ---
## Context
Found during raid 219-224 (2026-06-04) by the 0222 execute agent: a
stray src/go/git-erg binary left by `go build ./...` made the
offline-invariant check in tests/test_update.sh FAIL -- the grep for
net/http or crypto/tls scans src/go/ recursively and matched the
binary's debug symbols. The official build (make) strips symbols with
-s -w and outputs to build/erg, so it never produces that file, but
any developer or agent running `go build ./...` inside src/go/ trips
the suite. Test-isolation sharp edge, not a product defect.

## Actions
1. Restrict the offline-invariant grep in tests/test_update.sh to
   *.go files (e.g. `grep -rn --include='*.go' ...`), or exclude
   non-text/gitignored files.

## Test
With a fake binary file containing the bytes "net/http" planted in
src/go/, the suite passes; with a real `import "net/http"` added to a
.go file, the suite fails.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Stray compiled binary in src/go/ no longer fails test_update.sh
- [ ] The invariant still catches a real net/http import in a .go file
- [ ] make check passes
